{
  "answer_text": "Yes, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) changes the latency of LLM-generated answers, though the direction and magnitude of the change vary across different studies and datasets. The evidence shows that RAG can either increase or decrease latency compared to parametric-only (no-retrieval) baselines.\n\n**Increases in Latency:**\nIn several experiments, the retrieval-augmented model exhibited higher latency than the baseline:\n*   On **LawFactQA**, the retrieval-augmented generator had a latency of **1.68s** compared to **0.77s** for the closed-book model [S009, 1694-3107].\n*   On **GeoFacts**, the retrieval-augmented generator took **2.59s** versus **1.44s** for the closed-book model [S009, 1694-3107].\n*   On **HistoryQuest**, the retrieval-augmented generator had a latency of **2.51s** compared to **1.76s** for the vanilla LLM [S037, 1724-3172].\n*   On **LawFactQA**, the retrieve-then-read model took **1.25s** compared to **1.16s** for the vanilla LLM [S049, 1710-3124].\n*   On **OpenFactQA**, the retrieve-then-read model had a latency of **2.22s** compared to **1.69s** for the vanilla LLM [S049, 1710-3124].\n*   On **GeoFacts**, the retrieval-augmented model took **3.28s** compared to **2.85s** for the vanilla LLM [S080, 1834-3108].\n*   On **LawFactQA**, the retrieval-augmented model had a latency of **2.43s** compared to **2.03s** for the vanilla LLM [S080, 1834-3108].\n*   On **HistoryQuest**, the retrieve-then-read model took **2.72s** compared to **1.59s** for the no-retrieval baseline [S082, 1773-3214].\n*   On **LawFactQA**, the retrieval-augmented model had a latency of **2.71s** compared to **1.31s** for the vanilla LLM [S097, 1683-2845].\n\n**Decreases in Latency:**\nConversely, in other experiments, RAG resulted in lower latency:\n*   On **SciFactBench**, the retrieval-augmented model had a latency of **1.73s** compared to **1.77s** for the parametric-only model [S008, 1618-2906].\n*   On **OpenFactQA**, the RAG pipeline had a latency of **0.46s** compared to **1.62s** for the closed-book model [S030, 1835-3324].\n*   On **GeoFacts**, the RAG pipeline took **3.44s** compared to **1.25s** for the closed-book model, but in a different study on the same dataset, the retrieve-then-read model had a latency of **0.78s** compared to **2.16s** for the no-retrieval baseline [S030, 1835-3324] [S082, 1773-3214].\n*   On **TriviaCheck**, the retrieval-augmented generator had a latency of **2.61s** compared to **3.35s** for the vanilla LLM [S040, 1627-2889].\n*   On **HistoryQuest**, the retrieval-augmented generator took **2.15s** compared to **3.38s** for the vanilla LLM [S040, 1627-2889].\n*   On **BioClaimQA**, the retrieve-then-read model had a latency of **2.44s** compared to **2.55s** for the vanilla LLM [S033, 1492-2672].\n*   On **LawFactQA**, the retrieve-then-read model took **2.92s** compared to **1.79s** for the vanilla LLM, but in another study, the retrieve-then-read model on LawFactQA had a latency of **1.25s** vs **1.16s** [S033, 1492-2672] [S049, 1710-3124].\n*   On **NewsTruthQA**, the retrieve-then-read model had a latency of **1.28s** compared to **2.97s** for the vanilla LLM [S085, 1643-2916].\n*   On **OpenFactQA**, the retrieve-then-read model took **1.86s** compared to **2.86s** for the vanilla LLM [S085, 1643-2916].\n*   On **SciFactBench**, the retrieval-augmented generator had a latency of **1.47s** compared to **1.74s** for the vanilla LLM [S037, 1724-3172].\n*   On **OpenFactQA**, the retrieval-augmented model had a latency of **0.58s** compared to **2.01s** for the vanilla LLM [S097, 1683-2845].\n*   On **PopCultureQA**, the retrieve-then-read model had a latency of **1.77s** compared to **1.52s** for the closed-book model [S068, 2034-3484].\n*   On **OpenFactQA**, the retrieve-then-read model took **2.66s** compared to **2.84s** for the closed-book model [S068, 2034-3484].\n\n**Context:**\nSurveys note that retrieval latency is often reported separately from generation cost, and the total inference cost includes both the retrieval step and the generation step [S109, 0-1211] [S107, 1173-2028]. The variation in results suggests that the impact on latency depends on the specific implementation, dataset, and hardware used.",
